WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:06.935
"Now what?"

2
00:00:14.041 --> 00:00:19.946
said. He and his friends were huddled beneath some trees, hidden from the dragons flying overhead.

3
00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:22.848
"This is bad," Perda said.

4
00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:27.312
"We're lost, and we don't have any way to contact Arrano and the others."

5
00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:31.836
Just then a loud squawk came from directly above them.

6
00:00:33.104 --> 00:00:34.284
"It's the dragons!"

7
00:00:34.584 --> 00:00:35.165
Gliss cried.

8
00:00:35.185 --> 00:00:36.645
"They found us!"

9
00:00:37.805 --> 00:00:38.486
"No, wait."

10
00:00:38.906 --> 00:00:40.566
Darb peered up at the branches.

11
00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:43.147
"That didn't sound like a dragon."

12
00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.067
Zann looked up too.

13
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:48.108
A large bird was perched on an upper branch.

14
00:00:48.128 --> 00:00:52.189
"That looks a lot like Teplo's sniffer goose," Darb said.

15
00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:54.950
"Only smaller and with a shorter neck."

16
00:00:56.171 --> 00:00:56.931
Perda sighed.

17
00:00:56.951 --> 00:01:01.052
"This is no time for identifying native species, Darb.

18
00:01:01.932 --> 00:01:04.514
Besides, that goose doesn't look very friendly.

19
00:01:05.195 --> 00:01:06.236
Let’s get moving."

20
00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:10.179
She grabbed Darb's arm and started to drag him away.

21
00:01:10.199 --> 00:01:12.681
"Quiet!" Gliss warned.

22
00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.743
"Here comes a dragon."

23
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:19.768
Zann hid behind a tree as a medium-sized dragon walked past.

24
00:01:20.608 --> 00:01:24.331
With every step thick orange smoke puffed out of its nostrils.

25
00:01:24.352 --> 00:01:29.196
"This is crazy," Zann said once the dragon was out of sight.

26
00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:33.218
"We can't just wander around looking for that wormhole."

27
00:01:34.359 --> 00:01:35.720
"Yeah," Perda agreed.

28
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.863
"Besides, we'll have to use magic to levitate over the boiling lake anyway.

29
00:01:41.864 --> 00:01:44.085
Let's just save time and zap there."

30
00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:46.787
"We can't," Gliss said.

31
00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:48.649
"We're lost, remember?"

32
00:01:48.669 --> 00:01:52.251
"I can try a Seeking spell," Perda offered.

33
00:01:52.271 --> 00:01:55.693
"That's how I found the wormhole back in Swamp Bottom."

34
00:01:55.713 --> 00:01:58.275
"Good idea," Zann said.

35
00:01:58.295 --> 00:01:59.556
"Join friction."

36
00:02:00.436 --> 00:02:03.317
Perda, Gliss, and Zann rubbed their hands together.

37
00:02:03.337 --> 00:02:05.838
"Seek," Perda said.

38
00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:07.539
"It's working!"

39
00:02:08.219 --> 00:02:10.681
Zann could feel the magic energy tugging at him.

40
00:02:11.641 --> 00:02:14.882
The Seeking spell led them through the valley below the trees.

41
00:02:15.823 --> 00:02:20.285
Zann was climbing over some large rocks when he heard a rustling sound overhead.

42
00:02:21.525 --> 00:02:24.887
He looked up and saw a large dragon flying straight at them.

43
00:02:25.947 --> 00:02:26.988
"Everyone get down!"

44
00:02:27.248 --> 00:02:27.688
he shouted.

45
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.641
Zann threw himself behind a boulder.

46
00:02:31.661 --> 00:02:36.202
A blast of fiery air hit the spot where he'd just been standing.

47
00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.643
"I think that's a flame fury!"

48
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:39.323
Darb said.

49
00:02:39.343 --> 00:02:42.004
"Like the ones that powered the Dragon Wagon.

50
00:02:42.384 --> 00:02:43.744
They must come from this world!"

51
00:02:44.884 --> 00:02:46.785
"Great," Gliss said grimly.

52
00:02:46.805 --> 00:02:49.846
"All the more reason to get out of here!"

53
00:02:49.866 --> 00:02:52.807
"We'd better zap away," Zann said.

54
00:02:52.827 --> 00:02:56.828
"Zap!" He felt a twinge, but nothing happened.

55
00:02:57.636 --> 00:02:58.237
"Oh no!"

56
00:02:58.557 --> 00:02:59.117
Perda cried.

57
00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:02.360
"That Seeking spell used up our magic energy!"

58
00:03:03.321 --> 00:03:05.202
The fury was circling toward them again.

59
00:03:06.123 --> 00:03:08.504
Flames were already curling out of its snout.

60
00:03:09.285 --> 00:03:10.006
Darb stood up.

61
00:03:10.026 --> 00:03:12.087
"Darb!" Gliss cried.

62
00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:13.608
"Get down!"

63
00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:21.354
Cupping both hands around his mouth, Darb took a deep breath and let out a loud honking sound.

64
00:03:21.374 --> 00:03:23.516
"What are you—" Zann began.

65
00:03:24.008 --> 00:03:27.690
Suddenly an answering honk came from the direction of the trees!

66
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:34.052
A second later the goose flapped into sight and spit a blob of goo directly at the dragon.

67
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:39.134
The fury howled, falling to the ground with an earth-shaking thump.

68
00:03:40.055 --> 00:03:44.416
It pawed frantically at its face, trying to rub away the thick goose spit.

69
00:03:45.397 --> 00:03:46.917
"What are we waiting for?"

70
00:03:47.157 --> 00:03:47.758
Perda cried.

71
00:03:47.778 --> 00:03:53.400
"Run!" Zann took off with the girls at his heels and Zing flying overhead.

72
00:03:54.412 --> 00:03:58.513
Darb paused just long enough to give a honk of thanks and then followed.

73
00:03:59.493 --> 00:04:03.515
They'd only been running for a few minutes when they almost stumbled over a wormhole.

74
00:04:03.535 --> 00:04:07.676
"The Seeking spell found a different wormhole!"

75
00:04:07.896 --> 00:04:08.696
Gliss exclaimed.

76
00:04:09.456 --> 00:04:11.577
"Good," Perda said, panting.

77
00:04:11.597 --> 00:04:15.018
"We might not have enough energy left to levitate.

78
00:04:15.518 --> 00:04:18.699
And I definitely didn't feel like swimming in that lake again!"

79
00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:22.220
Darb cast a nervous glance over his shoulder.

80
00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.381
"I think I hear that dragon coming.

81
00:04:25.622 --> 00:04:28.423
Hurry!" Zann grabbed Perda's hand.

82
00:04:29.364 --> 00:04:32.465
Perda held out her hand to Gliss, who was holding Darb's hand.

83
00:04:33.126 --> 00:04:37.588
They all dived into the wormhole.

84
00:04:38.809 --> 00:04:41.330
Soon the friends were hurtling through the vortex.

85
00:04:42.471 --> 00:04:44.712
"Hold tight, everyone," Gliss said.

86
00:04:44.732 --> 00:04:48.954
"It makes me nervous to be here without our Shackle spell."

87
00:04:50.035 --> 00:04:51.456
"Hey, Darb," said Zann.

88
00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.982
"How did you know that goose would help us?"

89
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:59.166
"I remembered the fake snuffer goose from the Dragon Wagon," Darb explained.

90
00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:04.410
"When I realized we were in the furies' home world, I guessed that goose we saw must have

91
00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.150
been a snuffer."

92
00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.213
"But how did you know how to call it?"

93
00:05:08.373 --> 00:05:08.973
Perda asked.

94
00:05:08.993 --> 00:05:12.816
"Because of Teplo’s pet sniffer goose," Darb said.

95
00:05:12.836 --> 00:05:17.380
"I picked up a few words of its language while we were staying with Teplo.

96
00:05:18.548 --> 00:05:23.210
Since sniffer and snuffer geese look similar, I guessed their languages might be related."

97
00:05:24.511 --> 00:05:24.991
He shrugged.

98
00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.511
"Luckily, I was right."

99
00:05:26.531 --> 00:05:29.332
"Wow." Zann was impressed.

100
00:05:29.813 --> 00:05:31.373
He never would have thought of any of that!

101
00:05:31.393 --> 00:05:34.515
"You saved us from being roasted, Darb."

102
00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:36.915
"Yeah." Gliss shuddered.

103
00:05:37.516 --> 00:05:39.517
"Roasted and eaten."

104
00:05:39.537 --> 00:05:42.038
"Hey, Zann," Perda said.

105
00:05:42.058 --> 00:05:44.318
"Your purple marks are glowing again."

106
00:05:45.499 --> 00:05:47.980
Zann grabbed at the next wormhole and tumbled through it.

107
00:05:48.768 --> 00:05:53.369
Jumping to his feet, he was prepared to fight or run, but he quickly relaxed.

108
00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.770
This world didn't look scary at all.

109
00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.211
"Where are we?"

110
00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.251
Gliss wondered, climbing to her feet.

111
00:06:01.171 --> 00:06:01.892
Perda shrugged.

112
00:06:02.312 --> 00:06:04.472
"Wherever it is, it looks boring."

113
00:06:04.492 --> 00:06:12.955
"Yeah." Zann stepped away from the wormhole, which swirled shut and disappeared, leaving almost no color anywhere.

114
00:06:14.015 --> 00:06:20.774
Everything—the sky, the ground, the trees and shrubs—was dull shades of beige and gray.

115
00:06:20.794 --> 00:06:25.697
"At least there aren't any scary creatures attacking us," Gliss said.

116
00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:27.358
Darb nodded.

117
00:06:27.378 --> 00:06:29.700
"I don't see any signs of people either.

118
00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.822
How are we going to figure out if Wyssa's here?"

119
00:06:32.842 --> 00:06:35.483
"Zing!" Perda scolded.

120
00:06:35.503 --> 00:06:36.704
"Don't eat that.

121
00:06:37.064 --> 00:06:38.625
We don't know if it's safe."

122
00:06:39.526 --> 00:06:41.027
The dragon was nibbling on a leaf.

123
00:06:41.047 --> 00:06:43.889
"He must be hungry," Zann said.

124
00:06:43.909 --> 00:06:45.150
"I am too.

125
00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:48.272
Let's conjure some food while we figure out what to do."

126
00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:49.920
"I'll do it."

127
00:06:50.361 --> 00:06:53.142
Gliss rubbed her hands together, but nothing happened.

128
00:06:54.443 --> 00:06:54.983
She frowned.
